==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non}} ''*þes-'', ''þessi'' {{qualifier|neuter plural}}, {{m|non|sjá}} {{qualifier|nominative}},<ref name=gb>[http://books.google.se/books?id=vyOSYHXObjoC&pg=PA76&lpg=PA76&dq=sj%C3%A1+Old+Norse+etymology+demonstrative&source=bl&ots=3AqydwiXKT&sig=aHhOL9mT3LAREj0-EzH6_oDGBuc&hl=sv&ei=BI-ETryXJ8je4QT0grSGDw&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=6&ved=0CE4Q6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q&f=false Old English and its relatives, Google books]</ref> related to and from the same ultimate origin as the irregular inflection of Old Norse {{m|non|sá}}, a descendant from the likewise irregularly inflected {{der|is|gem-pro|*sa}}.<ref name=gb/> Cognate with Old English {{m|ang|þes}} and Old High German {{m|goh|dese}}.

